  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 303 PM EDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nMonday through Thursday Night...\n\nMoving into the new work week, a prolonged streak of dry and hot \nweather is expected as an impressive 594 dm upper ridge axis shifts \neastward over the Ohio Valley.  Mostly sunny days and mostly clear \nnights are expected through Thursday.  Max temperatures will likely \ncontinue to increase through the week.  Overall, still think that \nthe NBM blend is likely too aggressive over parts of the region.  In \ngeneral, the highest temperatures will be over our \nwestern/southwestern sections (mainly west of I-65 and south of the \nWK Parkway) with slightly lower highs across the Bluegrass where \nrecent heavy rainfalls have left the vegetative cover in better \nshape and more green.  Across the I-65 corridor and points \nwest/southwest, webcams show decent vegetative stress showing up \nfrom warm/dry conditions.\n\nHighs on Monday will likely be in the lower 90s in areas west of I-\n65 with upper 80s and lower 90s over the Bluegrass.  We'll see temps \nrise 1-2 deg/day in this pattern for Tuesday/Wednesday with highs of \n93-98 across the west, with 90-95 in the east.  Similar temperatures \nare expected on Thursday with 94-99 in the west/southwest and 90-95 \nin the east.  Dewpoints next week will mainly be in the 60s though \nthey may increase to the upper 60s by late week.  We're likely to \nsee good mixing during the afternoon resulting in dry air mixdown. \nDespite this, we'll see afternoon heat indices in the upper 90s to \nthe lower 100s.  Latest LREF probs show 30-40% chances of exceeding \n100F for heat indices across our southwest on Tuesday.  By \nWednesday/Thursday, there is a 50% chance of exceeding 100F for heat \nindices in areas west of I-65, but this increases to >70% in the \nBowling Green area.  We will not see much relief at night as \novernight lows will only cool into the lower 70s, but may remain in \nthe upper 70s to around 80 in the urban corridors.\n\nBased on the latest LREF probs, we're not likely to reach heat \nadvisory criteria next week (3h or more of 105F).  However, the \nduration of this event and subsequent impacts may require the \nissuance of Heat Advisories in later forecast packages.\n\nFriday and Saturday...\n\nToward the end of the week, the latest data continues to suggest \nthat the upper level ridge will begin to flatten and retrograde \nslightly westward.  A back door frontal boundary may try and attempt \nto drop south into the region.  In addition, we'll see several \nperturbations that will be rotating around the periphery of the \nridge axis and may bring a chance of showers/storms mainly to our \neastern areas.",
